# DTO Patterns and Best Practices

## Overview
DTOs (Data Transfer Objects) are used throughout the timesheet microservice to transfer data between layers while maintaining separation of concerns. They prevent entity serialization issues and provide a clean API contract.

## DTO Structure Patterns

### 1. Record-Based DTOs (Preferred)
```java
public record TimesheetRequestDto(
    @NotBlank(message = "Timesheet name is required")
    String name,
    
    @NotNull(message = "Candidate ID is required")
    Integer candidateId,
    
    @NotNull(message = "Job ID is required")
    Integer jobId,
    
    @Valid
    List<TimeLogDto> timeLogs
) {
    public TimesheetRequestDto {
        if (name == null || name.trim().isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Timesheet name cannot be null or empty");
        }
        if (candidateId == null || candidateId <= 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Candidate ID must be a positive integer");
        }
        if (jobId == null || jobId <= 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Job ID must be a positive integer");
        }
    }
}
```

### 2. Builder Pattern DTOs
```java
@Data
@Builder
@AllArgsConstructor
@NoArgsConstructor
public class BulkPermissionCheckRequest {
    @NotNull(message = "Items list is required")
    private List<BulkPermissionCheckItem> items;
    
    private BulkDataLoadingStrategy explicitStrategy;
    
    @Data
    @Builder
    @AllArgsConstructor
    @NoArgsConstructor
    public static class BulkPermissionCheckItem {
        @NotNull(message = "Entity is required")
        private Entity entity;
        
        @Valid
        @NotNull(message = "Permission check context is required")
        private PermissionCheckContext permissionCheckContext;
        
        @Valid
        @NotNull(message = "Access control metadata context is required")
        private AccessControlCheckMetadataContext accessControlCheckMetadataContext;
    }
}
```

## DTO Categories

### 1. Request DTOs
Located in `dto/` package, handle incoming data:
- **Validation**: Use Bean Validation annotations
- **Immutability**: Records provide natural immutability
- **Compact Constructor**: Validate input parameters
- **Nested DTOs**: Use `@Valid` for nested validation

### 2. Response DTOs
Handle outgoing data:
- **Structured Data**: Organize response data logically
- **Optional Fields**: Use `Optional<T>` for nullable fields
- **Nested Objects**: Include related data as nested DTOs
- **Pagination**: Include pagination metadata

### 3. Internal DTOs
Used for internal data transfer:
- **Context DTOs**: [BulkPermissionCheckContext.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/access_control/contract_staffing/dto/BulkPermissionCheckContext.java)
- **Permission DTOs**: [PermissionCheckContext.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/access_control/contract_staffing/dto/PermissionCheckContext.java)
- **Metadata DTOs**: [AccessControlCheckMetadataContext.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/access_control/contract_staffing/dto/AccessControlCheckMetadataContext.java)

## Validation Patterns

### 1. Bean Validation Annotations
```java
public record TimesheetRequestDto(
    @NotBlank(message = "Name is required")
    @Size(min = 1, max = 255, message = "Name must be between 1 and 255 characters")
    String name,
    
    @NotNull(message = "Candidate ID is required")
    @Positive(message = "Candidate ID must be positive")
    Integer candidateId,
    
    @Email(message = "Email must be valid")
    String email,
    
    @Pattern(regexp = "^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$", message = "Date must be in YYYY-MM-DD format")
    String startDate
) {
    // Compact constructor validation
}
```

### 2. Custom Validation
```java
public record TimeLogDto(
    @NotNull(message = "Start time is required")
    LocalDateTime startTime,
    
    @NotNull(message = "End time is required")
    LocalDateTime endTime,
    
    String description
) {
    public TimeLogDto {
        if (startTime != null && endTime != null && startTime.isAfter(endTime)) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Start time cannot be after end time");
        }
        if (startTime != null && endTime != null && 
            Duration.between(startTime, endTime).toHours() > 24) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Time log cannot exceed 24 hours");
        }
    }
}
```

## DTO Mapping Patterns

### 1. Manual Mapping
```java
@Service
public class TimesheetService {
    
    public TimesheetResponseDto createTimesheet(TimesheetRequestDto request) {
        // Manual mapping from DTO to entity
        Timesheet timesheet = new Timesheet();
        timesheet.setName(request.name());
        timesheet.setCandidateId(request.candidateId());
        timesheet.setJobId(request.jobId());
        
        // Save entity
        Timesheet savedTimesheet = timesheetRepository.save(timesheet);
        
        // Manual mapping from entity to response DTO
        return new TimesheetResponseDto(
            savedTimesheet.getId(),
            savedTimesheet.getName(),
            savedTimesheet.getCandidateId(),
            savedTimesheet.getJobId(),
            savedTimesheet.getCreatedAt()
        );
    }
}
```

### 2. Mapper Classes
```java
@Component
public class TimesheetMapper {
    
    public Timesheet toEntity(TimesheetRequestDto dto) {
        return Timesheet.builder()
            .name(dto.name())
            .candidateId(dto.candidateId())
            .jobId(dto.jobId())
            .build();
    }
    
    public TimesheetResponseDto toResponseDto(Timesheet entity) {
        return new TimesheetResponseDto(
            entity.getId(),
            entity.getName(),
            entity.getCandidateId(),
            entity.getJobId(),
            entity.getCreatedAt()
        );
    }
    
    public List<TimesheetResponseDto> toResponseDtoList(List<Timesheet> entities) {
        return entities.stream()
            .map(this::toResponseDto)
            .toList();
    }
}
```

## Bulk Operation DTOs

### 1. Bulk Request DTOs
```java
public record BulkTimesheetRequestDto(
    @NotEmpty(message = "Timesheet requests cannot be empty")
    List<TimesheetRequestDto> timesheets,
    
    @Valid
    BulkOperationOptions options
) {
    public BulkTimesheetRequestDto {
        if (timesheets.size() > 100) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Cannot process more than 100 timesheets at once");
        }
    }
}
```

### 2. Bulk Response DTOs
```java
public record BulkTimesheetResponseDto(
    List<TimesheetResponseDto> successful,
    List<BulkErrorDto> errors,
    BulkOperationSummary summary
) {
    public BulkTimesheetResponseDto {
        if (successful == null) successful = new ArrayList<>();
        if (errors == null) errors = new ArrayList<>();
    }
}
```

## Pagination DTOs

### 1. Pagination Request
```java
public record PaginationRequestDto(
    @Min(value = 1, message = "Page number must be at least 1")
    Integer page,
    
    @Min(value = 1, message = "Page size must be at least 1")
    @Max(value = 100, message = "Page size cannot exceed 100")
    Integer size,
    
    String sortBy,
    String sortDirection
) {
    public PaginationRequestDto {
        if (page == null) page = 1;
        if (size == null) size = 20;
        if (sortDirection == null) sortDirection = "ASC";
    }
}
```

### 2. Pagination Response
```java
public record PaginatedResponseDto<T>(
    List<T> data,
    int page,
    int size,
    long totalElements,
    int totalPages,
    boolean hasNext,
    boolean hasPrevious
) {}
```

